WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.200
The color changes based on
how light hits it.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.270
Oh, how pretty.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.000
Isn't it? It's a rare item. I'll sell it cheap.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.970
Rare, my ass. It's just an old-style
defective item.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.610
Say, you're quite knowledgeable, Mister.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.010
Is that so?

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.550
But it was interesting!

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.280
It has to look human, no, it has to be identical to
humans or it's meaningless.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.050
They're man-made things after all.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.150
I think it would be boring if they
were the same.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.490
Welcome, I'm loaded with Harakuro Soft's
latest thinking algorithm.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.030
Easy tuning is one of my special features.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.400
You can choose to create from an obedient
personality to an arrogant one.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.860
You can create any kind of personality
you have in mind!

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.010
We're currently in the middle of a cash
back rebate campaign!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.410
Well, you can create something similar,
just on appearance alone.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.010
However, what's inside the head
is another story.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.280
Hey, Harada!

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.880
Asakura?

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.280
Mano Asakura?

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.120
Long time no see. You look well.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.660
Yeah, so do you.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.130
To think, I'd run into you at
a place like this.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.430
Oh, could you be building androids?

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.540
Got a problem with it?

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.700
No, I just find it surprising.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.930
Hardware? Software?

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.570
Well, I specialize in hardware.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.010
AI, the artificial intelligence field is
lagging behind by ten years.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.850
While I'm at it, I'd like to see the
software worked on.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.310
Especially by you.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.090
Unfortunately, I don't have any
talent on that end.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.060
Well, I'm in a hurry, so...

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.260
What, already?

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.420
Even after you meet your
old flame like this?

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.130
Later. Let's go, Mikura.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.570
Hey, wait. Wait!

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.160
What's the deal, all of a sudden?

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.310
She was a classmate when I was a student.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.480
She said she was your girlfriend.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.480
That, and there was a subtle and vague
atmosphere between the two of you.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.080
It's a joke.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.550
A girl like her wouldn't even look at me.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.010
Well, that's true. I'm convinced.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.460
You know, becoming immediately
convinced by such a reason

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.260
is making me somewhat pissed.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.820
By the way, I was thinking about
something from earlier.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.150
Were you a hardware specialist?

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.230
Not really.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.600
Though, developing artificial intelligence
systems doesn't result in something sellable.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.640
Especially with your intelligence. I'm convinced.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.540
And I'm telling you, don't be convinced
by such reasons!

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.810
That's my life's work!

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.240
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.020
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.990
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.760
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.460
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.330
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.530
You just barely escaped with your life

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.860
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.130
We're thirsty

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.060
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.270
Extremities and infinity

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.400
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.630
Together, they form a fantasy

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.300
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.500
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.330
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.560
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.560
<i>Wink</i>

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.630
Wink

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.240
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.450
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.580
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.880
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:10.490
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:10.690
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:19.390
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:19.630
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:26.700
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:26.900
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.170
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.370
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:35.640
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.710
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:40.010
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:40.150
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:48.440
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:48.990
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.960
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.160
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.960
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.130
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.630
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.900
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:59.260
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.570
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:07.870
<i>Shell of Memories</i>

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:20.360
Today's guest is the successor to the
late Dr. Mikijiro Asakura,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.160
who passed away a few days ago.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.290
As his successor, at a young age,

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.290
she was inaugurated as Asakura Technology
Research's representative supervisior,

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.960
Ms. Mano Asakura.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.450
Hey!

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:36.640
By burying plant seeds created through
biotechnology in your scalp,

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.440
your hair will be revived!

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.610
However, due to this being plant based,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.010
it'll be green, but dyeing is possible
so there's no worry.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:45.650
What?

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.050
If you call now, we'll include the sunlight,
which promotes photosynthesis.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:57.680
Does that mean I need to be prepared to turn my
head into a potted plant? Oh, please.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.090
Harada!

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.830
Oh, Mikura. It's almost time for dinner.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.100
Where's Harada?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:04.730
Harada?

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:06.460
Oh, I think he's downstairs.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.040
Hey, if you change it without permission,

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.710
then I'll find that regrettable.
The personality changed.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.280
Ms. Asakura is also the number one
researcher in robotics research.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.210
We met this woman today.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.050
She's Harada's classmate.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.540
Oh, Harada?

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.580
Asakura?

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.420
Oh...

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.320
That's nostalgic.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:27.480
Hot, ouch!

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.290
Yeah, the only daughter of the Asakura
Technology Research.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:35.300
If that's the case, if we ask, won't she
sell us some parts for cheap?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.630
You joke.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.190
She's the last woman I wanted to see.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:41.100
Because something happened?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.670
Someone poor like me isn't comfortable

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.370
around high society girls like her.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.430
We're poor, that's why I'm telling you this.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.050
I forgot to buy the eight inch control spindle!

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.410
This is meaningless without it!

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.850
Manon? Hey!

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.550
Don't touch something belonging to
others without permission.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.260
That's memory, isn't it?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.820
Is Manon that person?

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.760
Unrelated. This is read, "M-ANON."

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.760
How suspicious! Maybe it has memorable
photos on it or something?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:13.130
And at night, you gaze at them in secret
and think of your youth gone by.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.140
That doesn't suit you!

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.600
Say whatever you please.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.670
Both of you.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.110
Dinner is served, please come and get it.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.340
If it gets cold because you don't come,
don't blame me.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.410
All right! All right!

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.670
You don't need to say it twice.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:36.520
Moreover, we superficial humans forget
things just as monkeys do.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.560
The four or five years of time passed

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:45.090
attempted to cleanly remove my memories
of you from my heart.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:49.270
Little by little, you crossed over the
threshold of my consciousness,

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:52.730
on your way to becoming hidden in the
depths of my subconscious.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.480
Within this not so short amount of time,

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:59.240
there were significant changes
taking place with me.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.820
She was the campus's most
accomplished student

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:06.190
and the daughter of the president of Asakura
Technology Research, a global company.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.160
The young woman's name was Mano.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:12.630
Of course, I certainly wasn't
someone suited for her.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.700
Nevermind the fact I knew that
more than anyone else.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:19.220
I had feelings of love toward this
cool and beautiful girl.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.970
Here she comes...

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.200
Go, Harada!

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.200
Yeah.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:24.940
I changed my mind after all.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:26.370
What are you chickening out for?

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.400
Give it your best shot, Harada!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.680
I already know I'm going to fail.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.720
You know, in the end...

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.920
Here she comes!

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.990
Go! Do your best!

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.150
Whoa, ho, ho!

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.530
I wonder what she'll say to reject him?

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.150
No, I'm guessing she won't even give
him the time of day.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:48.550
All right.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.590
You want to go on a date with me
on the next day off, right?

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.710
Hey, don't you think something's strange here?

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.440
Yeah, definitely.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.810
All right!

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:08.150
Say what?!

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.980
I am not convinced!

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:13.010
Since she said okay to the likes of you, I
should have asked her out myself!

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.020
It's really worth giving it your best shot!

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.230
I wonder if it was a joke after all?

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.240
Yeah, that's got to be it.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.530
Harada?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.410
Asakura, right?

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.440
I'm sorry for being late.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:40.880
Are you mad?

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.180
Oh... No, not really.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:46.310
Great! I thought you'd yell at me.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.190
What's the matter?

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:54.650
Well, you seem quite different than
when we're at school and all.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.230
Really?

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.670
Anyway, hop on.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.400
We're riding this?

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.770
Oh, wait, your skirt.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.110
Sorry for not thinking about that ahead of time.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.310
We'll leave the bike here...

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:11.440
You're letting me ride with you!

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.240
I'm so happy.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.620
Are you sure about this? Really?

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.720
Hurry up and drive, Harada!

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.890
It's fast! Fast!

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.240
I don't understand her at all.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.010
You only took her for a ride
on your motorbike?

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.840
Well, yeah, we took one lap and then
went our separate ways from there.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.380
She dumped you.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.350
She had business to take care of!

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:51.880
Hi!

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:58.790
I thought so!

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.860
It looks like the dream ended in one night.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.130
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:08.830
Harada...

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.270
What is it?

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:14.610
I want to keep school and my
private life separate.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.740
Separate?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:23.810
I'm always getting attention from the
teachers and the students.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:28.050
Really, I'd rather not be bound
by things like that, but...

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.230
If it's you, I think you'll understand.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.260
That's why,

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.920
from now on, at school, I'd like us to act as
though we're complete strangers.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.300
What do you mean, from now on?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:42.440
Your motorbike, it was fun. Give me a ride again.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.810
I'll give you a ride anytime!

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.810
Thank you.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:54.010
After that, I was with Manon every day.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.260
Wow!

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:07.750
This is the first time I've seen this. lncredible.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:12.790
First time? You could see this
anytime, can't you?

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.100
No, because I hardly ever go outside.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.940
I guess high society girls have it rough too.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.910
Yeah, high society girls have it rough.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:26.140
Hey, don't make it sound like you're the victim.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.620
Right back at you! Poke!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:36.780
See you.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.500
Say, Asakura.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.260
Call me Manon.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:55.280
Manon, why did you go out with me?

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:58.470
I don't know, but I'm glad it was with you.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.840
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:08.550
Boom!

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:23.300
Is it really okay? Your not
eating anything, that is.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:26.710
Yeah, I'm okay with just watching you.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:32.750
But not eating out at all makes you seem
like the ultimate high society girl.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.480
I eat properly before leaving
and after I get back.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.990
In reality, could you be eating enough
for three people?

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:40.460
Poke!

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.550
Hey, don't do that when I'm eating!

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.730
Well, it's always only four hours, on the mark.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:51.000
I'm sorry. I have a lot of things to do.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.160
Oh, well.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:56.400
If I don't eat this in a hurry, I'll just waste time.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:15.010
I'm done.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.610
Oh, my, that was fast, pointy-head.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:20.390
There's a part I forgot to purchase.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.560
If I don't go in a hurry, the stores will close.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.230
You can do that tomorrow.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:28.200
I'm going to use them as repair parts
for goods I'm delivering tomorrow.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:29.900
Anyway, I'm off.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.640
He's really a workaholic.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.480
That's because you're not bringing in work

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.620
for the company like you're supposed to.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:44.190
Oh, my, now you're putting me in a spot
and painting me into a corner.

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:46.020
I wonder if I should take a part-time job too?

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:48.290
Don't take a job where your customers
are mainly middle-aged men.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:51.260
Come to think of it, I'm middle aged too,
but don't take such a job.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.450
I am done with my meal.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.300
Say, Pops!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:05.810
Oh... Say, Asami!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.270
Good evening.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.210
What are you doing at this hour?

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.550
Nothing.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.750
Mikura's in the office.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.980
Mr. Harada, where are you going?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.780
I'm going to do some shopping.
Want to go with me?

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:28.530
I see, even if you go home, you'd be alone.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.390
Both my parents are both busy with their work.

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:35.830
Then don't hesitate and come to the office.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:37.770
But...

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:40.570
I'll register your fingerprint so feel
free to come on in.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.780
But I always seem like I'm in your way.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.840
Well, it's our line of work. There's
a lot of dangerous stuff.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.620
Everyone's just concerned for your safety.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:15:00.950
Anyway, I'll copy your fingerprint
so stick your finger here.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.970
Hey, what are you doing?

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.300
Finger.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.000
That's not it.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.410
Poke.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.810
If you don't listen to what I want,
I'll poke you again.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.180
But the time...

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.550
But I want to ride that.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.220
We should come back for it next time.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.520
If you break curfew, you'll be in trouble, right?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.750
It doesn't matter. I want to ride it now.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.880
But...

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.630
Please, Harada!

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:38.860
Well, if you insist, that's fine with me.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:48.400
Wow! It's all red!

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:11.330
Harada, thank you.

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.830
This was really fun.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:17.200
What are you being so formal for?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.260
I'll never forget this scenery.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.340
Manon? Your eyes, just now...

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.070
Huh? What?

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.840
Well, nevermind.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.910
You're weird. Poke!

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:38.480
We wasted an hour.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.790
Hey, what's the matter? Hey!

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:44.560
Look out!

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:49.300
Hey, Manon! Are you feeling ill?

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:50.600
Manon!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:56.410
I'm Asakura Technology Research
Facility's M-ANON9993.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.380
What are you talking about?

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:00.310
To the person who finds me,

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:03.480
it may be a little bit of trouble,
but please immediately contact

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:06.040
the nearby Asakura Technology
Research Facility.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:12.090
I'm Asakura Technology Research
Facility's M-ANON9993.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.550
To the person who finds me...

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:14.550
What the hell is this?

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:24.200
You must be Mr. Harada. I'm
Mano Asakura's father.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.310
I really appreciate all your cooperation.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.700
Cooperation? What are you talking about?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.380
lnstead of that, what happened to her?

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:36.740
Come with me.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:48.250
Manon, you're...

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:52.590
I'm sorry. Things turning out like this
was outside of our calculations.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:56.270
Today, I was supposed to say goodbye to you

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:57.940
and the experiment would have been over.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:00.200
What are you saying? What are
you talking about?

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.370
Manon?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.180
I'm not the one who was meeting you.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:17.450
M-ANON9993, it's our company's
trial production android.

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.790
Android? Robot?

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.860
This can't be happening, because...

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:27.100
She didn't return by curfew
so her battery ran out.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:32.140
We didn't think she'd take actions
beyond our predictions.

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:36.940
This is to be celebrated. Humans are
the ones guided my emotions.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:42.350
As for the AI for the M-ANON project, it could be
said that it is as complete as a human being.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:45.390
Coming into contact with people

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.660
who don't notice anything and
naturally blending in,

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.250
this was the project's final phase.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.430
We apologize for using how you
felt about her for it.

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.900
We fully intend to compensate you well for this.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:59.230
Manon...

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:01.100
You're a robot?

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:05.490
Mr. Harada, M-ANON isn't there.
That's just a container.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:07.830
A container?

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:09.440
Come over here.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:16.440
Functioning. All green. M-ANON9993, AI system.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:18.170
Manon?

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:22.990
Harada! You're there? Why?

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:25.860
Please step back a little further.
Her eye is there.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.160
It's you, Harada, after all!

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.300
I'm sorry for surprising you.

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:33.900
When I was told I'd have to say goodbye to you
today, I wanted to be with you a little longer.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.240
I really wanted to stay with you
until my battery died.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:42.340
But it did die after all. I'm such a klutz.

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:49.220
Say, Harada? Why do you look so sad?

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:53.740
Did I say something bad? I'm sorry.

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:58.960
I thought you were human all this time.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.430
I can't believe this.

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:03.300
Really? I'm so happy!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:07.770
I was ordered to make you believe
I was human for the duration.

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.870
I was scared at first, but...

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.770
You turned out to be a lot nicer than I thought.

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:18.780
But I'll never forget the glowing red
scenery we saw on the Ferris wheel.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.880
Thank you, Harada.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:24.250
You're really Manon.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:28.320
Yes, but I can't poke you anymore

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:31.550
and I'm going to miss having you
poke my cheeks.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.800
Father, I think that's a reaction more
than enough for a human.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:42.630
Yes, when I heard your plans,
I did have my doubts.

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:47.610
By examining the experience data and
analyzing the algorithms,

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:50.980
we can make an android with an
intelligence just like a human.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.450
Don't screw with me!

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:54.320
As a human, my ass!

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:58.910
Do you guys have any idea how this makes
me feel? You gotta be kidding me!

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:00.690
What are you doing?!

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:01.780
Stop it!

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.400
Mano, security, call security! No, the police!

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.090
Before that, get the data!

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:16.770
Harada, what's the matter? What are you doing?

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:18.070
Damn it!

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:24.170
I don't understand. Why are you
breaking things?

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:27.820
Sorry, even I don't know.

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:30.580
Harada, tell me...

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.780
Ha... ra... da...

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:34.710
Manon!

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:42.260
There he is!

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:44.230
Hey, you! Are you all right?

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:52.100
You overdid it. I guess there was something
that broke the camel's back.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.570
Say, Mr. Harada?

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:01.280
Are you dating Ms. Mikura?

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:03.820
What's this, all of a sudden?!

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:05.890
Well, I did wonder about it, so...

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:07.420
Does it look like we are?

00:22:07.420 --> 00:22:09.120
No, not at all.

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:10.610
I see.

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:13.790
What's this?

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:17.000
It looks like android personality synchro data.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.860
So what is that?

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:21.570
Memories, personality,

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:24.400
it's a record of an android's individually
distinguished characteristics.

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.210
Hey, it's no good. Crud. Hello?

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:28.410
Is it broken?

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.510
It seems like it's data to be loaded
into a pretty specialized system.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:31.850
It wants to see. It wants to listen.
It wants to speak.

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:33.480
I see. And here I was, looking forward to

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:36.210
some compromising photos between
Harada and his old girlfriend.

00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:38.910
Your personality is quite twisted, indeed it is.

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:43.220
The system Harada wrecked at
Asakura a while back...

00:22:43.220 --> 00:22:47.060
Come to think of it, that was considered a loss
on a national level, or something.

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:51.390
Say, Mr. Harada, is making androids fun?

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:53.990
You have an interest?

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:56.340
That's not it.

00:22:57.140 --> 00:22:59.940
Something like that is a little scary.

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:01.900
Scary...

00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:05.470
It just might be.

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:10.150
<i>Shell of Memories</i>

